CORE
main.c
--no-por --unwind 2 --rounds 3 --index-chain --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^index chain: [1-9][0-9]* of
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The read takes the index the chain holds at its position and then the value of
the write with that index. Verified by mutation: decoding index k to the value
of write k+1 makes the read see main's later write of 5, and this test then
reports VERIFICATION FAILED.
